<title>FRANCE: Belgian Renault workers clash with French police.</title>
<headline>Belgian Renault workers clash with French police.</headline>
<dateline>LILLE, France 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Four Renault workers were injured on Thursday when strikers from the car company's Belgian plant tried to force their way into the mayor's office in Lille, northern France, police said.</p>
<p>Police said 300 demonstrators protesting against Renault's plan to close the Vilvoorde plant had sought a hearing with Lille Mayor Pierre Mauroy, a former prime minister. After learning that Mauroy was in Paris, they tried to force their way into city hall and broke windows, prompting police to intervene.</p>
</text>
